## Hypotheses

### Hypothesis 1

The current `-129.90%` drawdown remains less severe than previous cycle lows.

One possible interpretation is that the correction may still be incomplete.

This is not evidence of continuation — only a structural observation.

---

### Hypothesis 2

If prior cycle behavior repeats in a comparable form, the local Momentum bottom of the current correction could potentially fall somewhere in the:

```text
-66,000 to -80,000
```

This is not a statistical projection or quantitative model.

It is only a rough assumption based on prior cycle structures.

---

## Sample Size Limitation

Only `4` completed historical cycle observations exist in this dataset.

Any conclusions derived from it should be treated with caution due to the extremely limited sample size.

